  "raw": {
    "https://mitchell.libguides.com/facultystafftech": {
      "title": "Faculty/Staff Apps Homepage",
      "description": "Apps Homepage - Faculty/Staff Apps Homepage - LibGuides at Mitchell College Skip to Main Content Skip to main content My Library Account Home Articles Books & Videos Guides Citations Services About Faculty/Staff Apps Homepage The tools and support you need at Mitchell College. Apps Homepage Library Resources Teaching & Learning Support This link opens in a new window Apps Support Toggle Dropdown Blackbaud (Faculty Portal) Follett & Course Resources This link opens in a new window Moodle (Open LMS) Office 365 & OneDrive Zoom This link opens in a new window Microsoft 365 Your Microsoft Network Account Use your Microsoft 365 Network Account to access most Mitchell systems . Don't know your account information? Contact OIT: support@mitchell.edu, 860-701-5190. Mitchell Email/Outlook Log in with your email address and network password. Expired or forgotten password? Reset here. Instructional Apps (Moodle) Log in with your network username and password. Additional support is available online or in person. Faculty Portal Log in with your Mitchell email address and password ( instructions here ). View rosters, take attendance, and enter midterm and final grades. Insight for Faculty Report academic concerns to the advising team. Syllabus Library Access the current syllabus template then upload your syllabus (for each course, every term) Learn about the Division chair review and approval process. Need a syllabus not found in the Syllabus Library?  Contact the Moodle administrator. Administrative Apps Login requires a Mitchell network account unless otherwise noted. Accommodate by Symplicity Learning accommodations management; access is based on college role. ADP Self-Service Payroll and benefits management; login provided by Human Resources. Paycom is replacing ADP; refer to communication from HR for details. Paycom Payroll and benefits management; login provided by Human Resources. Paycom is replacing ADP; refer to communication from HR for details. Advocate by Symplicity Student conduct management; access is based on college role. Planning & Accreditation Strategic planning, targets, and outcomes. Access is based on college role. Blackbaud.com Includes Education Management, Raiser's Edge, and Financial Edge. Detailed login instructions here ; access is based on college role. Event Manager Reserve campus spaces and schedule related event support (room setup, dining, and IT). Follett Textbook Adoption Resources Adopt textbooks so they will appear in the college's online bookstore Log in with your self-registered account and password (Mitchell email recommended) Genio Notes (formerly Glean) Notetaking and transcription tool for students.  Faculty can share content and view usage. Accounts created by invitation from Accessibility Services (pilot program). Insight for Staff Set up office hours for students to view; report academic concerns Students can schedule appointments with tutoring, advisors, and library support online Marketing & Communications Requests Request marketing and communications support including website updates. Papercut - FollowMe Printing Print from any device by downloading the mobility print app Qualtrics Survey and data reporting tool. Access is granted upon approval. Go directly to Qualtrics. RAVE Alert Campus-wide emergency notifications. Register using your Mitchell email address. Residence by Symplicity Residence Life management. Access is based on college role. Work Orders Facilities-related requests. Access is based on college role. Slate Admissions and financial aid management. Access is based on college role. Student Code of Conduct Also available to students from the Current Students homepage. 3rd Millennium Classrooms Prevention and intervention courses.  Access is based on college role. Transportation Requests Schedule group transportation to and from off-campus locations. UCM iContracts Login provided by the Business Office. Access is based on college role. Zoom Licensed accounts are assigned by OIT. Username/password is defined by the individual user (not network-connected). Password Reset Microsoft 365 Password Reset Passwords must be changed every 180 days. If your password stops working, try a reset. Mitchell College Strategic Plan Strategic Plan 2022-2027 This link opens in a new window Illuminating Mitchell College's Future Mitchell College Brand Standards Mitchell College Brand Guide This link opens in a new window Mariner Athletics Brand Guide This link opens in a new window Library & Instructional Technology Support Contact us. The library staff is here to support you in using the college's technology and information resources. Department & Group Sites Access to these sites is based on college role (contact OIT for assistance). Academic Advising This link opens in a new window Assessment This link opens in a new window BLC-SIS This link opens in a new window Business Office This link opens in a new window Campus Safety Banned List This link opens in a new window College Policies This link opens in a new window Committees This link opens in a new window Faculty Review This link opens in a new window Human Resources This link opens in a new window Internal Communications This link opens in a new window Accounts & Campus Technology Visit the OIT Service Desk Portal Student Support The CARE (Campus Assessment, Response, Evaluation and Support) Team at Mitchell College offers coordinated support for students in distress, addressing concerns related to student behavior, academic progress, and personal issues, including mental health challenges. CARES Group: Submit A Referral Request This link opens in a new window Referral Chart Last Updated: Jun 16, 2026 9:31 AM URL: https://mitchell.libguides.com/facultystafftech Print Page Login to LibApps Report a problem Subjects: Technology How-to"
    },
    "https://mitchell.edu/integrative-career-development/": {
      "title": "Integrative Career Development",
      "description": "Integrative Career Development Integrative Career Development // 860-701-5000 admissions@mitchell.edu Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Youtube Facebook Instagram LinkedIn Youtube Alumni Giving Parents Faculty & Staff Students Why Mitchell Teaching Adaptability Playing to Your Strengths Celebrating Diverse Thinkers At A Glance Thames at Mitchell College The SAILS Program A Message from President Espy Academics Academic Calendars Academic Calendar 2026/27 Academic Calendar 2025-26 Professional Studies Calendar 2026-2027 Professional Studies Calendar 2025-2026 Undergraduate Programs Applied Exercise Science Business Management Criminal Justice Digital Communication Early Childhood Education First-Year Experience General Education Health Sciences Honors Program Individualized Studies Marine and Environmental Science Minors Nursing Professional Studies – Business Professional Studies – Health and Human Services Psychology Sport Management Graduate Program Academic & Social Support Accessibility Services Advising The Bentsen Learning Center The SAILS Program Thames at Mitchell College Tutoring Center Career: Integrative Career Development Dual Enrollment College Catalog Intersession Library Meet Our Faculty Mitchell Ability Model Registrar Summer Internships Summer Courses Jumpstart Program Thames at Mitchell College Student Life Resources Life at Mitchell Performing Arts Health & Wellness Campus Safety Title IX and Non-Discrimination Policy Activities Bookstore Gear Store Dining Services Athletics Athletics Continuing Education Mitchell Hub: Digital Innovation & Educational Excellence STAIRs News & Stories News & Stories Public Spaces Children’s Learning Center Event & Meeting Space Rentals Michael’s Dairy Mitchell Beach The Red Barn Pop-up Gear Shop Admissions Visits & Events Visits & Events Campus Map & Directions Request Information Accepted Students Adult Learners Apply to Mitchell Apply to Thames Cost & Financial Aid Transfer Students School Counselors Veterans Meet the Team Select Page Integrative Career Development Career Support at Mitchell The relationship between career and Mitchell College in one word? Solid. Career is solidly embedded in the Mitchell College experience. It’s a career immersion model that relies on strong community partnerships and it goes well beyond the typical career office you find at most colleges. With our distinctive Mitchell Ability Model and Integrative Career Development (ICD) program, learning – and networking – extends beyond the classroom from your first semester on campus. By partnering with leading Southeastern Connecticut organizations through ICD, students get… behind the scenes observation first -year through last -year networking opportunities hands-on career experience throughout their time on campus It’s real-world. It’s relevant. It’s immersive. And we will prepare you well for engaged citizenship in Southeastern Connecticut. Applying Abilities to Career Through the Mitchell Ability Model, students are continuously applying what they are learning in the classroom to career opportunities on campus and in the field. Integrative Career Development coordinates numerous experiences over all 4 years and prepares students to engage fully in each opportunity: 4-Year Plan for Career Success Explore our 4-Year Plan for Career Success that takes students from developing a job search strategy to growing their network of professional contacts to gaining critical experience through internships — and beyond. First Year First Year students embark on self discovery and build academic skills while exploring career through: learning their individual strengths and interests connecting with our regional partners and developing an understanding of career opportunities Third Year Third year students are selecting their Core area of academic study and beginning to explore possible majors. In preparation for career, students are applying Abilities they are mastering to: on-campus career labs such as the Children’s Learning Center internships projects and volunteering enrichment activities or specialized courses in high-interest areas Second Year Second year learning focuses on the 7 Essential Abilities and transferable skills. Career exploration this year includes: resume writing interviewing & business etiquette networking and partner mentors field trips and job shadowing aligning career path with personal strengths and interests Fourth Year Fourth year students continue their Core study and develop specialized skills in any chosen majors. Students continue skills-building and further refine career goals by: applying abilities to on-campus career labs and internships networking with regional ICD partners taking advantage of local job fairs, alumni panels and professional speakers setting professional or grad school goals Internships Internships are an invaluable component of career development. According to the New England Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) Class of 2017 Student Survey Report , “each graduating class from 2013-2017 has had at least 60% of students participate in an internship and/or co-op at some point in their college career.” And according to their Job Outlook 2017 Survey Report, 65% of employers prefer their candidates to have relevant work experience and 56% prefer the experience comes from an internship or co-op . At Mitchell College, we go well beyond the internship or co-op experience to create “pathways to employment” that begin in the very first semester and become progressively more complex and engaging every academic year. Faculty members and Integrative Career Development staff help students connect to the opportunities that are right for them. From résumé writing and interview practice to one-on-one support matching students to our dynamic partner sites, the process is guided, allowing students to explore the professional world confidently. Visit mitchell.edu/stories to learn how Mitchell students are applying knowledge to internships, projects and research. Summer Internships Learn More Contact ICD Office Hours: Monday – Friday: 8:30am-12:00pm and 1:00-5:00pm. Duques Center, 2nd Floor Through CSM Symplicity at https://mitchell-csm.symplicity.com/students/ Please take a moment to complete a quick survey if you have had a recent appointment with the ICD office.  We appreciate your participation! Employers interested in posting an internship or job opportunity may register for an employer account through https://mitchell-csm.symplicity.com/employers/ or can contact: Paul Dunn, ICD Coordinator Duques Center 213 860-701-7739 dunn_p@mitchell.edu Student Links Resume Writing Interviewing Networking College Central Student Job Board Workforce Recruitment Program for College Students with Disabilities Student Stories Visit mitchell.edu/stories to learn how Mitchell students are engaged in our region through internships and research experiences. Alumni Career Services Career services don’t end when you earn your Mitchell degree. ICD offers continuing services to Mitchell alumni, including: + resume and cover letter review + job search + networking strategies + interview preparation and more! Internship Stories Matthew Keatley Internship Solidifies Career Goals Kyrsten Lucas Securing a Competitive Pfizer Internship Sevda Kalican One Step Closer to Achieving Career Goal Internship Partners Mitchell College ICD partners with leading Southeastern Connecticut organizations to enhance its academic programs and increase pathways to professional employment. By collaborating with dynamic, successful organizations, the College can benefit the community and best prepare its graduates for engaged citizenship in Southeastern Connecticut. List of Partners Chamber of Commerce of Eastern Connecticut Connecticut Department of Children and Families Fellowship House Ministries Flock Theatre G’s Fitness and Nutrition Garde Arts Center Greater Mystic Chamber of Commerce Harbor Elementary School High Hopes Therapeutic Riding Mohegan Sun Mystic Aquarium Mystic Marriott Hotel & Spa Mystic Seaport Nathan Hale Arts Magnet School New London Recreation Department Norwich Sea Unicorns Norwich Youth & Family Services Regional Multicultural Magnet School Pfizer Safe Futures SARAH Inc. St. Edmund’s Retreat on Enders Island The Arc Eastern Connecticut The Day The Friendship School The Spa at Norwich Inn United States Coast Guard Academy Alumni Association Veolia Vista Life Innovations Waterford Youth & Family Services 10/15/25 Partner With Us! Employers may inquire about partnering with ICD or posting an internship or job opportunity by contacting: Paul Dunn, ICD Coordinator Duques Center 213 860-701-7739 dunn_p@mitchell.edu Supporting Internships: The Robert Andrew Cohen Internship Fund Robert “Robbie” Cohen ’15, who passed away in 2020, was known to many as the “Mayor of Mitchell College,” an individual with a deep commitment to service and a supporter and friend to countless peers. He achieved his dream of a Walt Disney World internship and, after graduation, went on to his career in hospitality at Disney in Orlando, Florida, where he received numerous customer service awards. Thanks to generous anonymous donors, Mitchell College is honored to offer students the support and freedom to pursue internships to write their own story, as Robbie did. The Robert Andrew Cohen Internship Fund provides financial support for current students or recent graduates, immediately after their senior year, who pursue non-paid and/or low paying internships. Funds give students the opportunity to develop industry-specific skills and professional experience, while defraying the costs associated with completing an internship opportunity. How to Apply Application period for Fall 2026: Coming Soon Internship students can submit a request for funds for: Housing Travel Wages Other expenses associated with the internship opportunity ICD Staff Paul Dunn Integrative Career Development Coordinator dunn_p@mitchell.edu 860-701-7739  Connect with ICD on Facebook  Connect on LinkedIn  Connect on Twitter  Connect on LinkedIn  Connect with ICD on Facebook  Connect on Twitter Apply to Mitchell! The process is simple. Get started now Mitchell College 437 Pequot Avenue New London, CT 06320 860-701-5000 admissions@mitchell.edu APPLY NOW! Campus Safety Careers Contact Us Privacy Policy Terms & Conditions Title IX & Non-Discrimination Web Accessibility Close the accessibility toolbar Accessibility visibility_off Disable flashes title Mark headings settings Background Color zoom_out Zoom out zoom_in Zoom in remove_circle_outline Decrease font add_circle_outline Increase font spellcheck Readable font brightness_high Bright contrast brightness_low Dark contrast format_underlined Underline links font_download Mark links Reset all options cached Manage Cookie Consent To provide the best experiences, we use technologies like cookies to store and/or access device information. Consenting to these technologies will allow us to process data such as browsing behavior or unique IDs on this site. Not consenting or withdrawing consent, may adversely affect certain features and functions. Functional Functional Always active The technical storage or access is strictly necessary for the legitimate purpose of enabling the use of a specific service explicitly requested by the subscriber or user, or for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network. Preferences Preferences The technical storage or access is necessary for the legitimate purpose of storing preferences that are not requested by the subscriber or user. Statistics Statistics The technical storage or access that is used exclusively for statistical purposes. The technical storage or access that is used exclusively for anonymous statistical purposes. Without a subpoena, voluntary compliance on the part of your Internet Service Provider, or additional records from a third party, information stored or retrieved for this purpose alone cannot usually be used to identify you. Marketing Marketing The technical storage or access is required to create user profiles to send advertising, or to track the user on a website or across several websites for similar marketing purposes. Manage options Manage services Manage {vendor_count} vendors Read more about these purposes Accept Deny View preferences Save preferences View preferences {title} {title} {title} Manage consent"
